++USERMOD(ZMG0003)      /* IKJCT441 FOR REXX */ .
++VER(Z038) FMID(EBB1102) PRE(ZP60038)
 /*
   PROBLEM DESCRIPTION:
     THE VARIABLE ACCESS ROUTINE IKJCT441 OF ZP60038 SERVES CLIST
     VARIABLES ONLY, SO ISPF DIALOG VARIABLES DO NOT WORK FROM A
     REXX EXEC.

     THIS USERMOD ADDS A REXX PATH.  WHEN ECTENVBK (ECT+X'30')
     POINTS TO A REXX ENVIRONMENT BLOCK, IKJCT441 CALLS THE VARIABLE
     ROUTINE IN THAT BLOCK.  THE ROUTINE DECIDES WHO IS SERVED: WITH
     RC -1 NO EXEC IS RUNNING AND THE CLIST PATH RUNS UNCHANGED.
     WITHOUT SUCH A BLOCK IKJCT441 BEHAVES AS IN ZP60038.

   SPECIAL CONDITIONS:
     ACTION:
       RUN THE MEMBERS OF THE LIBRARY USERMOD.ZMG0003 IN THIS ORDER:
       ZMG03CK (CHECK), ZMG03BK (BACK UP IKJPTGT), $INSTALL (ASSEMBLE,
       RECEIVE, APPLY CHECK), ZMG03AP (ASSEMBLE, APPLY).  ZMG03RS
       REMOVES THE USERMOD AGAIN.
     ACTION:
       IKJPTGT IS IN THE LINK PACK AREA.  THE USERMOD BECOMES ACTIVE
       WITH THE NEXT IPL WITH CLPA, AND SO DOES ITS REMOVAL.
     ACTION:
       DO NOT ACCEPT THIS SYSMOD.  IT STAYS REMOVABLE WITH RESTORE.
     DEPENDENCY:
       REXX VARIABLES NEED A REXX IMPLEMENTATION THAT PUBLISHES ITS
       ENVIRONMENT BLOCK WHILE AN EXEC RUNS.  BREXX/370 DOES THIS FROM
       3.1.0 ON.  UP TO 3.0.1 IT KEEPS ECTENVBK ZERO AND THE CLIST
       PATH RUNS AS BEFORE.
     PREREQUISITES:
       ZP60038, WHICH REQUIRES ZP60014 AND UY01301.
     RESTRICTION:
       THE ENVIRONMENT BLOCK MUST STAY VALID WHILE IT IS IN ECTENVBK.
       A PRODUCT THAT LEAVES A BLOCK THERE AFTER ITS CODE IS UNLOADED
       MAKES EVERY LATER CALL OF IKJCT441 ABEND UNTIL LOGOFF.

   COMMENTS:
     IKJCT441 FOR REXX, MVSLOVERS, BY MIKE GROSSMANN.  THE CLIST PATH
     IS THE ONE OF ZP60038 BY GREG PRICE.  COMBINES WITH ZMG0001 AND
     ZMG0002: IT CHANGES NONE OF THEIR ELEMENTS.
     ZMG01CK OF BREXX/370 3.0.0 LISTS ZMG0003 AS A USERMOD THAT MUST
     NOT BE INSTALLED.  THAT MEANT AN OLDER PLAN AND DOES NOT APPLY.

     THE FOLLOWING MODULES ARE AFFECTED BY THIS USERMOD:
     MODULES:
       IKJCT441
     LOAD MODULES:
       IKJPTGT (SYS1.LPALIB)
 */ .
++MOD(IKJCT441) DISTLIB(AOST4) TXLIB(IKJCT441) .
